\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 3\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Arrays\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Arrays are like groups of variables that allow you to store sets of similar data\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab A single dimension array is useful for storing and working with a single set of data\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab A multidimensional array can be used to store and work with multiple sets of data\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Array programming techniques covered\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab Summing and averaging all the elements in an array\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab Summing all the columns in a two-dimensional array\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab Searching an array for a specific value\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab Using parallel arrays\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 4\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Array Characteristics\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab An array stores multiple values of same type\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab Like a group of variables with a single name\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab For example, the days of the week might be:\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab A set of 7 string variables\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab With a maximum length of 9 characters\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab All variables within an array are called elements and must be of the same data type\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab You access the elements in an array through a subscript\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 5\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Declaring an Array\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Declare an array much like a regular variable\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab ArrayName is the name of the array\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab UpperSubscript is the value of the array's highest subscript\par
\pard\tx1080\li1080\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab Must be a positive Integer\par
\pard\tx1080\li1080\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab Positive Integer named constant\par
\pard\tx1080\li1080\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab Integer variable containing a positive number\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab DataType is a Visual Basic data type\par
