\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab A two-dimensional array declaration requires two sets of upper subscripts\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab First upper subscript is for the rows\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Second upper subscript for the columns\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab ArrayName is the name of the array\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab UpperRow is the value of the highest row subscript\par
\pard\li360\sb60\sa140\f1\fs22\cf5 {\cf5 Must}{\cf5  }{\cf5 be}{\cf5  }{\cf5 a}{\cf5  }{\cf5 positive}{\cf5  }{\cf2 integer}\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab UpperColumn is the value of the highest column subscript\par
\pard\li360\sb60\sa140\f1\fs22\cf5 {\cf5 Must}{\cf5  }{\cf5 be}{\cf5  }{\cf5 a}{\cf5  }{\cf5 positive}{\cf5  }{\cf2 integer}\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab DataType is the Visual Basic data type\par
